Faithful-parity note: the web <Checkbox> is a PURE presentational control with NO fetch / hooks, so it has
no loading/error/stale/offline branch (nothing to fetch, fail, age, or lose connectivity to). Inventing
such chrome would fabricate states the source does not have, so this surface reproduces only the source's
REAL branches (unchecked / checked / indeterminate / disabled / sizes / labelled-unlabelled) — exactly as
the sibling presentational primitives ActiveFilterChips (0147), Delta (0081), MetricCard (0095) did.
The web source has NO t() keys (anonymous surface); the only user text is the caller-supplied label. The
Checkbox.strings keys are native accessibility additions (the spoken state a browser derives for free from
<input type=checkbox>'s checked/indeterminate), required so the native control is never silent to VoiceOver.

